cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this harness, these measurements, or this paper, please cite it
  using the metadata below. If you cite a specific number, please cite the
  finding it comes from as well: every figure in the paper traces to a record
  in results/, and findings/ records what each one does and does not establish.
title: >-
  What You Are Actually Measuring When You Benchmark Speculative Decoding
  Under FP8: A measurement case study on vLLM 0.29.0 and NVIDIA L4
abstract: >-
  An independent measurement study of speculative decoding and FP8
  quantization on vLLM 0.29.0 / NVIDIA L4 (SM89). Four confounds are
  identified and quantified: attention-backend selection is conditioned on
  KV-cache dtype, so a precision A/B is also a kernel A/B; speculative
  throughput falls into one of two disjoint regimes, and an intervention on
  rented hardware shows the deficit regime depends on the serverless
  platform it was measured on, not on the driver alone; acceptance length
  has a boot-to-boot CV below 0.88% in all nine sessions measured; and
  "inter-token latency" computed from stream-arrival timestamps is
  inter-chunk latency under speculation, which inverts a p95-ITL goodput
  ranking rather than merely adding error to it. Released with the harness,
  the raw append-only records, the analysis scripts, and 45 findings,
  including formal retractions and revisions of earlier readings.
